#
#  A list of allowable sky boxes. One is picked at random at server start; declare only
#  one if you want a specific sky.
#
#  A SKYBOX LABEL SETS THE SKY AND NOTHING ELSE. Every label here used to end in
#  `if client_id==0: music_schedule_random()`, because scheduling a skybox runs its body
#  and nothing anywhere else ever chose a track - so an empty body meant a silent game,
#  and a mod adding skies had to copy the incantation or break the sound. Music is now
#  chosen on its own, from the MUSIC_SELECT setting, a map's `Defaults:`, or the server
#  console's Music dropdown. See sbs_utils procedural/media.py.
#
#  A label body still RUNS when its skybox is scheduled - put anything genuinely
#  sky-specific in one. Note it runs per client, so guard with `if client_id==0:` for
#  anything that should happen once.
#

#
#  The music banks this mission offers. `music_get_list()` reads these, so they are what
#  the console dropdown shows; MUSIC_SELECT names one of them (or "random").
#
@media/music/default "Cosmos Default Music"
@media/music/Artemis2 "Classic Artemis2 music"


@media/skybox/sky1  "Default red"

@media/skybox/sky1-blue "Cosmos"

@media/skybox/sky1-ds9 "subdued blue"

@media/skybox/sky1-rainbow "Rainbow"

@media/skybox/sky-bored-alice "borealis"

@media/skybox/sky-delight "Sailor's delight"

@media/skybox/sky-neb2-rvb "Red vs. Blue"
